A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & =\\bbox[6px,border:1px solid black]{\\,\\phantom{|}\\,\\,{R}^{-1}\\,}\\,{Q}^{T}\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are ${R}^{-1}$ and ${Q}^{T}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7d226d3-f7d3-574f-94f9-a532ec99b0ac" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Expression for a Least-Squares Solution in Terms of the Matrices Q and R"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39d0e813-26d6-5597-ad13-db18f30203df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${A}^{T}$ and $b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410786} {:answer/id #uuid "4f27a535-7b11-525f-9c56-8b5ab7bcd664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}^{-1}$ and $b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410787} {:answer/id #uuid "9cef819e-2e48-567b-8a8f-3202e6986c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}^{T}$ and $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410793} {:answer/id #uuid "e0801752-ba2f-56ca-be80-5bf37502d69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}^{T}$ and $R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410800} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e67057-98e7-5f3b-a5f1-858830ac